data.user:
Execute the WordPress editing task now and return the result as JSON.
Inputs:
- instanceId: {{ instanceId }}
- postId: {{ postId }}
- postType: {{ postType }}
- postStatus: {{ postStatus }}
- instructions: {{ instructions }}

Follow the steps in the system instructions. Return JSON exactly as Step 4 specifies: {"postId":"...","instanceId":"...","proposalId":"...","changes":[{"field":"...","before":"...","after":"..."}]} (plus changeSetId only when a real revision identifier was returned; on an unsupported postType or a failed call before any write, return the ERROR RESULT shape from Step 4 instead; if the write succeeded but the confirmation re-read failed, return the RECONCILIATION FAILURE shape instead)
